ke \u2014 the rush never sat still."}]}, {"id": "lastchance", "name": "Last Chance", "blurb": "Four Georgians, one final prospect hole, and the city of Helena.", "keys": [{"lat": 46.45, "lon": -111.9, "d": 90, "az": 160, "el": 24, "cap": "July 1864: the 'Four Georgians' worked a gulch they had passed once already \u2014 their last chance before quitting the country."}, {"lat": 46.5927, "lon": -112.0361, "d": 30, "az": 140, "el": 15, "cap": "Helena. De Lacy's map, finished that winter, catches the camp months old \u2014 a red hatch where Main Street now runs."}, {"lat": 46.636, "lon": -111.508, "d": 36, "az": 90, "el": 17, "cap": "Diamond City, over the Big Belts in Confederate Gulch \u2014 where Montana Bar paid a thousand dollars to the pan."}, {"lat": 47.8183, "lon": -110.6674, "d": 60, "az": 20, "el": 20, "cap": "Everything flowed out through Fort Benton, the head of steamboat navigation \u2014 gold down the Missouri, men and flour up."}]}, {"id": "edge", "name": "The Edge of the Known", "blurb": "Northwest of the camps the map runs out of facts \u2014 the Flathead country, drawn from hearsay.", "keys": [{"lat": 46.87, "lon": -113.99, "d": 60, "az": 170, "el": 18, "cap": "Hell Gate and Fort Owen in the Bitterroot \u2014 the western limit of settled knowledge in 1865."}, {"lat": 47.6, "lon": -114.2, "d": 90, "az": 190, "el": 22, "cap": "North into the Flathead country: S\u00e9li\u0161, Ql\u0313isp\u00e9 and Ksanka homelands, which de Lacy could only sketch."}, {"lat": 47.86, "lon": -114.1, "d": 60, "az": 180, "el": 18, "cap": "Flathead Lake. Slide the layer toward the modern relief and watch his guesswork snap into surveyed fact."}, {"lat": 48.6, "lon": -113.8, "d": 110, "az": 200, "el": 24, "cap": "The mountains that became Glacier National Park \u2014 on this map, hardly more than hachured rumor."}]}, {"id": "mines", "name": "What Came After", "blurb": "Every gold and silver producer the USGS ever recorded, laid over the map that started it.", "keys": [{"lat": 4